onchain.example_query:
TESTED, returns real fills for our btc-updown-5m window. Endpoint: https://1rpc.io/matic (no API key). Window blocks: start 88701137 (ts 1781756701) .. end ~88701290 (ts >1781757000); 50-block max per call so paginate.

curl -s -X POST https://1rpc.io/matic -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{
  "jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_getLogs","params":[{
    "fromBlock":"0x54978d1",
    "toBlock":"0x5497902",
    "address":"0xE111180000d2663C0091e4f400237545B87B996B",
    "topics":["0xd543adfd945773f1a62f74f0ee55a5e3b9b1a28262980ba90b1a89f2ea84d8ee"]
  }]
}'

Decode each log: maker = '0x'+topics[2][-40:]; taker = '0x'+topics[3][-40:]; data split into 32-byte words -> w[0]=side, w[1]=tokenId, w[2]=makerAmountFilled, w[3]=takerAmountFilled, w[4]=fee. Keep logs where w[1] == our clobTokenId. Result above: slice returned 3709 fills, 1939 of them carrying our YES/NO tokenIds.

For NegRisk markets swap address to 0xe2222d279d744050d28e00520010520000310F59. To find fromBlock/toBlock for an arbitrary window, binary-search eth_getBlockByNumber on timestamp (done here: ts 1781756700 -> block 88701137).

(The Goldsky GraphQL equivalent below is provided for completeness but returns [] for our window because the indexer is frozen at 2026-04-28:)
POST https://api.goldsky.com/api/public/project_cl6mb8i9h0003e201j6li0diw/subgraphs/orderbook-subgraph/0.0.1/gn
{"query":"{ orderFilledEvents(first:1000, where:{makerAssetId:\"<tokenId>\"}){ timestamp orderHash maker taker makerAssetId takerAssetId makerAmountFilled takerAmountFilled fee } }"}
